 "fixed_skill": "Fixed investigation skill\n\nPurpose\nInterpret the known state of an outage investigation using text and structured\nobservations. Separate mapped geography from measured coverage. Pre-outage target\ncoverage identifies potentially affected locations; the down cell cannot be an\navailable backup after its outage.\n\nEvidence rules\nOnly queried locations with valid records provide coverage evidence. An unqueried\nlocation and a queried location with missing data both have unknown coverage, but\ntheir query progress differs. A valid empty cell list means no cell coverage.\nA valid nonempty list without the target is a different observation. Do not invent\nsignal measurements for absent cells. Population and complete demand cannot be\ninferred from residential land-use tags. Other land-use types do not imply zero\ndemand. Known geographic boundaries do not imply known coverage inside them.\n\nSpatial interpretation\nUse the stated coordinate units and the available geometric references. A road\ncenterline is not an area: use its declared buffer to query a road corridor.\nQuery-frontier locations are selected by adjacency between queried and unqueried\ngrid locations within a declared reference, independently of signal values.\nMissing frontier data must not be counted as proof that target coverage ends.\nCounts from overlapping references cannot be summed as disjoint areas.\n\nTools\ncoverage.query accepts a geographic reference resolved to its geometry and actual\ngrid identifiers. Use existing resolvable references; do not invent coordinates or\nreference identifiers. Inspect result status and separate complete valid records\nfrom missing records. Preserve links to observations for evidence provenance.\nimpact.estimate selects eligible backups and estimates synthetic traffic transfer\nunder explicitly stated thresholds, scope, units, and load formulas. Exclude the\ndown cell. Keep location share distinct from traffic share and report unserved\ndemand and excluded unknown locations. Do not interpret a demonstration formula as\na calibrated network model or claim use of a KPI absent from the formula.\n\nState and history\nState describes current known facts and remaining unknowns; it does not prescribe\nan action. A step records one executed action and its result. A trace orders steps.\nThe context preview records what was available before an action, not necessarily\na request sent to a model. Human maps are supplementary artifacts; text-only\ndecision makers must use state and observations, not image paths as evidence.\nThe end of a script does not prove investigation sufficiency. Do not infer unknown\ncoverage, future results, or a complete outage impact from partial observations.\n",
